---
import '../styles/global.css';
import model from '../../model/dynamos-v2.json';

const rawBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = rawBase.endsWith('/') ? rawBase : `${rawBase}/`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Responsible use, scope, limitations, and liability statement for DYNAMOS."
    />
    <title>Responsible Use — DYNAMOS</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href={base}>DYNAMOS</a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href={base}>Home</a>
        <a href={`${base}model/`}>Model</a>
        <a href={`${base}#precepta`}>PRECEPTA</a>
        <a aria-current="page" href={`${base}responsible-use/`}>Responsible use</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="legal-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Scope, boundaries & responsibility</p>
        <h1>Responsible use of DYNAMOS</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          DYNAMOS is intended for reflection, communication, education, research,
          and system-aware design. It is not a diagnostic, clinical, evaluative,
          or decision-making instrument.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-grid">
        <aside class="legal-summary">
          <p class="eyebrow">In short</p>
          <p><strong>DYNAMOS does not diagnose.</strong></p>
          <p><strong>DYNAMOS does not assess fitness, ability, or worth.</strong></p>
          <p><strong>DYNAMOS should not determine consequential decisions about a person.</strong></p>
        </aside>

        <article class="legal-copy">
          <section>
            <h2>Intended use</h2>
            <p>
              DYNAMOS is a reflective and research framework for describing how a
              cognitive-behavioral system may operate under meaning, load,
              interaction, context, and time. Its outputs are conditional,
              context-dependent descriptions intended to support reflection and
              communication rather than verdicts about individuals.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Not a diagnostic or clinical instrument</h2>
            <p>
              DYNAMOS is not a medical, psychological, psychiatric, diagnostic,
              clinical, or psychotherapeutic instrument. It does not diagnose or
              rule out autism, ADHD, or any other condition. It does not produce
              a clinical threshold, probability of diagnosis, or substitute for
              assessment by an appropriately qualified professional.
            </p>
            <p>
              DYNAMOS is not currently a validated psychometric diagnostic
              instrument and should not be represented as one.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Not for consequential decisions</h2>
            <p>
              DYNAMOS results must not be used as the sole or determinative basis
              for medical treatment, diagnosis, hiring, dismissal, promotion,
              grading, selection, exclusion, legal decisions, accommodation
              determinations, or access to services.
            </p>
            <p>
              The framework is not a performance evaluation and does not establish
              a person's competence, suitability, reliability, productivity, or worth.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Professional support</h2>
            <p>
              Anyone seeking advice concerning health, diagnosis, treatment,
              psychological support, legal rights, workplace accommodations, or
              other professional matters should consult an appropriately qualified
              professional in the relevant jurisdiction or field.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Interpretation limits</h2>
            <p>
              DYNAMOS describes tendencies and configurations rather than fixed
              traits. No single dimension defines a person or pattern. The same
              observable behavior may arise from different underlying mechanisms,
              and the same underlying configuration may present differently across
              contexts, relationships, and time.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
            <p>
              DYNAMOS and the materials provided through this project are supplied
              <strong>“as is”</strong>, without warranties regarding accuracy,
              completeness, fitness for a particular purpose, diagnostic validity,
              or suitability for any particular decision.
            </p>
            <p>
              To the extent permitted by applicable law, the author and contributors
              are not responsible for decisions, actions, losses, damages, or other
              consequences arising from the use, misuse, interpretation, or reliance
              upon DYNAMOS or materials derived from it.
            </p>
            <p>
              Users remain responsible for how they apply the framework and for
              obtaining appropriate professional advice where required.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Privacy and examples</h2>
            <p>
              Public DYNAMOS examples should be synthetic or clearly documented
              composites unless there is an explicit and appropriate basis for
              publication. Identifiable personal, clinical, workplace, or educational
              information should not be added to public DYNAMOS materials without
              appropriate permission and safeguards.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Research status</h2>
            <p>
              DYNAMOS is an open theoretical and reflective framework. Its public
              specification can be inspected, questioned, tested, and adapted.
              Claims about reliability, validity, population norms, diagnostic
              accuracy, or predictive performance require empirical evidence and
              must not be inferred from the existence of the framework itself.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="legal-note">
            <h2>Legal note</h2>
            <p>
              This page states the intended scope and conditions of use of DYNAMOS.
              It is not legal advice, and nothing on this page overrides rights or
              obligations that apply under relevant law.
            </p>
          </section>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div>
        <p>
          <strong>DYNAMOS — Dynamic Neuro-Operational Systems Model</strong><br />
          © {model.copyright.year} {model.copyright.holder}
        </p>
        <p>
          Except where otherwise noted, DYNAMOS model content is licensed under
          CC BY-SA 4.0.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-notice">
        <p><strong>Responsible use:</strong> non-diagnostic, non-clinical, and not a substitute for professional advice.</p>
        <p><a href={base}>← Return to DYNAMOS</a></p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
